"— ","Directly supported by the figure — 29 and 26 percent versus 12 percent."]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mr-1 font-bold text-eng-green-700","children":["B","."]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"italic text-eng-navy-500","children":"Moving midday slots to the evening has reduced the clinic's unused-slot rate."}]," ","— ","Correct — this is the unsupported one. The passage explicitly says results are not yet available."]}],["$","li","2",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mr-1 font-bold text-red-700","children":["C","."]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"italic text-eng-navy-500","children":"The clinic's staff expectation about early appointments was not borne out by its own data."}]," ","— ","Supported by paragraph 2 read against the figure."]}],["$","li","3",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mr-1 font-bold text-red-700","children":["D","."]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"italic text-eng-navy-500","children":"The clinic attributed midday no-shows to conflicts with work shifts."}]," ","— ","Supported by paragraph 3, which gives the clinic's explanation."]}]]}]]]}]]}]
41:["$","section","vd-challenge",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-3 font-display text-lg font-bold text-eng-navy-900","children":"Challenge"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-2","children":[["$","details","vd-c1",{"className":"group rounded-xl border border-eng-navy-200 bg-white","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start gap-3 rounded-xl p-4 font-medium text-eng-navy-900 focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-eng-teal-600","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-0.5 shrink-0 rounded bg-eng-navy-100 px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-bold text-eng-navy-700","children":["Q",1]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"flex-1 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed","children":"In paragraph 1 of Text A, the coordinator writes that between March and June, \"monthly visits grew by more than half.\" Which calculation from the figure correctly checks this claim?"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"shrink-0 text-eng-navy-400 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180","aria-hidden":"true","children":"▾"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"border-t border-eng-navy-100 p-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-3 rounded-lg bg-eng-green-50 p-3 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-900","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold text-eng-green-700","children":["Correct answer:"," "]}],"D. 520 − 340 = 180, and 180 is more than half of 340, so the claim is supported."]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-800","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold","children":"Why: "}],"Find the two months the claim names — March at 340 and June at 520 — and subtract: 520 − 340 = 180. Growing \"by more than half\" compares the increase to the starting value, and half of 340 is 170. Since 180 is more than 170, the figure supports the claim. Notice what the claim and the figure both count, though: visits."]}],[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-2 mt-4 text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-eng-navy-500","children":"Every choice, explained"}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"space-y-2","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mr-1 font-bold text-red-700","children":["A","."]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"italic text-eng-navy-500","children":"520 − 310 = 210, and 210 is more than half of 310, so the claim is supported."}]," ","— ","The conclusion is right, but the numbers are not. 310 is the January bar; the claim starts in March, so the starting value must be 340."]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mr-1 font-bold text-red-700","children":["B","."]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"italic text-eng-navy-500","children":"480 − 340 = 140, and 140 is less than half of 340, so the claim is not supported."}]," ","— ","480 is the April bar. The claim runs to June, so the ending value must be 520. Stopping one month early makes a supported claim look unsupported."]}],["$","li","2",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mr-1 font-bold text-red-700","children":["C","."]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"italic text-eng-navy-500","children":"520 − 340 = 180, but 180 is less than half of 520, so the claim is not supported."}]," ","— ","The subtraction is right, but the comparison uses the wrong base. Growth is measured against where visits started, 340 in March, not where they ended. Half of 340 is 170, and 180 is more than that."]}],["$","li","3",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mr-1 font-bold text-eng-green-700","children":["D","."]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"italic text-eng-navy-500","children":"520 − 340 = 180, and 180 is more than half of 340, so the claim is supported."}]," ","— ","Correct. March is 340 and June is 520, an increase of 180. Half of 340 is 170, so an increase of 180 is more than half."]}]]}]]]}]]}],"$L50","$L51","$L52"]}]]}]
